  "prefLabel": "Env-Or 302.58 Unusual operating condition",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Or 302.58 “Unusual operating condition” means any condition, equipment deficiency, or occurrence that results or could result in a release of oil, indicates the possibility of a system leak, or creates a reasonable expectation that a system leak is imminent. Examples of unusual operating conditions are listed in Env-Or 306.07(a).\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Or 300) #10487, eff 2-7-14; ss by #14094, eff 10-4-24 (formerly Env-Or 302.57)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-or300.html"
